			<div class="content" id="post-content-4175275">
									

<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">This is missing a rating module.</span></p>
<p>I don't dislike this enough to downvote, but I will say this is dense and difficult to read, especially considering how straight-forward the anomaly is. I feel like with some tweaking this could be a -J. It's an anomaly that forces people to use corporate jargon, and it can be written with corporate jargon, like in the interview at the end. If it's going to be on the main list, it just needs more to it than &quot;corporations be crazy&quot;.</p>
<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Also, if this anomaly actually has the capability of affecting the top 500 corporations, then it is Keter. That is a lot of data to track and contain. Think of the amount of resources it would take to monitor ALL of the corporate communications at, say, Wal-Mart. Then add 499 more corporations of that size to that list. We're talking about an anomaly that affects the vast majority of the American work force plus a huge chunk of overseas workers too.</span></p>
<p>On a second reading, it's not that bad. Thanks for taking my feedback into account though. It makes me feel special.</p>

